      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <climits>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n            scanf(\"%d\", &matrix[i][j]);\n\n    // Integral image with two parallel phases: row-wise prefix then column accumulation\n    std::vector<std::vector<long long>> ps(n + 1, std::vector<long long>(n + 1, 0));\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long sum = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            sum += matrix[i][j];\n            ps[i + 1][j + 1] = sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int j = 1; j <= n; ++j) {\n        for (int i = 2; i <= n; ++i) {\n            ps[i][j] += ps[i - 1][j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    #pragma omp parallel for collapse(2) reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(runtime)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n            long long sum = ps[i + s][j + s] - ps[i][j + s] - ps[i + s][j] + ps[i][j];\n            if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n        }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Parallelize integral image construction using two phases of work sharing (row-wise prefix sums and column accumulation) with explicit static scheduling. Use collapse(2) reduction(max) on the search phase with runtime scheduling to demonstrate thread granularity control.",
  "notes": "The row-wise prefix sum loop is parallel over rows, each computing its own cumulative sum independently. The column accumulation loop is parallel over columns, adding contributions from previous rows sequentially within each column. Both use schedule(static). The final search uses collapse(2) reduction(max) with schedule(runtime), allowing the runtime environment to control chunk size and scheduling policy.",
